<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="SweetChorus-G-Theme" spTempo="142">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1936 (first recorded)
Composer:	Django Reinhardt
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	32-bar AABA
Style:	Gypsy jazz; swing
Key:	G major

“Sweet Chorus” is an instrumental by Django Reinhardt,
first recorded in Paris in October 1936 with the Quintette
du Hot Club de France. Reinhardt recorded it again in 1947;
the tune’s chart centers on G major.</spComments>
